page('ways-we-help.html', 'Ways we help', f'''<div class="wrap"><section class="sub-hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">Ways we help</div><h1>Recognize the snag?<br>See a way through.</h1></div><div class="description"><p>Start with the work that gets stuck—not a list of technologies.</p><p class="tiny">Illustrative scenarios, not client results. The right fix depends on your people and tools.</p></div></section><div class="filter-bar"><div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter examples by industry"><button data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">All examples</button><button data-filter="trades" aria-pressed="false">Trades</button><button data-filter="property" aria-pressed="false">Property management</button><button data-filter="marine" aria-pressed="false">Marine services</button></div><span class="tiny" data-example-count role="status">9 possibilities</span></div><div class="example-grid">{items}</div><div class="two-col"><h2>Your business doesn’t fit<br>one of these labels?</h2><div><p>These are starting points, not the limits of the business. Enquiries, handoffs and follow-through show up in many kinds of work.</p><a class="text-link" href="contact.html">Tell us where it gets stuck ↗</a></div></div></div>''' + closing())

page('how-it-works.html', 'How it works', '''<div class="wrap"><section class="sub-hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">How it works</div><h1>One useful fix.<br>Then build from there.</h1></div><div class="description"><p>No giant replacement project. We start with the tools you already use and the people who know the work.</p></div></section><div class="process-grid"><article class="process-card"><span class="number">01 / DISCOVER</span><h2>Find the snag.</h2><p>Walk through a real example. Map the people, tools and handoffs. Check whether a simpler process or a setting in your existing software is enough.</p><p class="deliverable">You get: a clear recommendation, even if you choose not to build.</p></article><article class="process-card"><span class="number">02 / DEPLOY</span><h2>Make the connection.</h2><p>Agree one result, a fixed scope and a price. Build it, test the ordinary cases and exceptions, then walk your team through what changed.</p><p class="deliverable">You get: the agreed system, operating notes and a human fallback.</p></article><article class="process-card"><span class="number">03 / CARE</span><h2>Keep it useful.</h2><p>If you choose care, we maintain the agreed connections, investigate issues and make included small adjustments. New capabilities are scoped separately.</p><p class="deliverable">You get: clear ownership and agreed support boundaries.</p></article></div><div class="two-col"><h2>The judgment stays<br>with your people.</h2><div><p><strong>We can organize the information. You decide what to promise.</strong> Pricing, scheduling tradeoffs, sensitive messages and exceptions stay with the people who understand the business.</p><p>AI is an option, not a requirement. Access, compatibility and data handling are checked before a solution is agreed.</p></div></div><div class="two-col"><h2>Yours to understand.<br>Not a black box.</h2><div><p>You receive the agreed documentation and handoff. We identify account ownership, ongoing software costs and how to pause or transfer the system.</p><a class="text-link" href="pricing.html">See the prices and boundaries ↗</a></div></div></div>''' + closing())

page('pricing.html', 'Pricing', '''<div class="wrap"><section class="sub-hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">Pricing, in plain numbers</div><h1>Know the price.<br>Know what’s included.</h1></div><div class="description"><p>A focused first project, with discovery counted in. Agree the result and the boundaries before work starts.</p><p class="tiny">Proposed pricing for this design study; subject to scope and a written agreement.</p></div></section><div class="price-grid"><article class="price-card"><div class="eyebrow">01 / Discovery</div><h2 style="margin-top:18px">Find the right first fix.</h2><div class="price">$999</div><p>Understand the current work and choose a worthwhile starting point.</p><ul><li>Current workflow and tool review</li><li>One recommended first improvement</li><li>Written scope and next-step options</li></ul><p class="price-note">The $999 is credited once toward your first deployment. The assessment remains useful if you stop here.</p></article><article class="price-card featured"><div class="eyebrow">02 / First deployment</div><h2 style="margin-top:18px">Put one fix to work.</h2><div class="price">$2,499 <span>total</span></div><p><strong>$1,500 remaining</strong> after the discovery credit. Not $2,499 on top.</p><ul><li>One clearly scoped business result</li><li>Agreed connections and acceptance tests</li><li>Documentation and team handoff</li></ul><p class="price-note">Data migration, new locations, complex access and broader workflows may need a separate scope.</p></article><article class="price-card"><div class="eyebrow">03 / Optional care</div><h2 style="margin-top:18px">Keep it running.</h2><div class="price">$499<span>/month, from</span></div><p>Support for the first agreed deployment after launch.</p><ul><li>Agreed checks and issue investigation</li><li>Connection upkeep</li><li>Included small adjustments</li></ul><p class="price-note">Coverage, response expectations, usage allowances and third-party fees are agreed in writing. Not unlimited development or 24/7 human support.</p></article></div><div class="extras"><div><h3>A larger first deployment</h3><p>$4,999 total is an example for broader initial scope—not a universal cap. The same discovery credit applies once.</p></div><div><h3>Another useful fix</h3><p>Additional deployments from $999, plus $249/month additional care, when existing connections and patterns can be reused. Otherwise, we rescope first.</p></div></div><section class="faq"><h2>A few straight answers.</h2><details><summary>Do we need to replace our software?</summary><p>Not usually the starting point. We inspect your current tools and permissions first. A native setting or a process improvement may be a better choice than adding a system.</p></details><details><summary>What does “one deployment” mean?</summary><p>One separately useful business result, with a named trigger, finished state, tools, rules, volume, exclusions and acceptance tests. It is not every individual technical step.</p></details><details><summary>Why is a later deployment less expensive?</summary><p>It can reuse connections and delivery patterns we already understand. But a later request can still be more complex; “from $999” is not a promise to build anything for that amount.</p></details><details><summary>What happens if we don’t buy care?</summary><p>You still receive the agreed system, documentation and handoff. Continued operation depends on the accounts, licenses and integrations involved. Ongoing responsibilities are made clear before work starts.</p></details><details><summary>Can I book through this concept?</summary><p>Not yet. The next-step page is a preview only, with no calendar, CRM or backend. Nothing is sent, and no appointment is booked.</p></details></section></div>''' + closing())

page('contact.html', 'Let’s talk', '''<div class="wrap"><section class="sub-hero"><div><div class="eyebrow">A useful first conversation</div><h1>Where does the<br>work get stuck?</h1></div><div class="description"><p>A real example is the best place to start. No polished brief required.</p></div></section><div class="contact-layout"><aside class="contact-context"><span class="preview-label">DESIGN PREVIEW · NOT A BOOKING FORM</span><h2>Start with the snag.<br>Not the software.</h2><p>In a fit conversation, we’d ask what happened last time, who was involved and what a useful next step would look like.</p><p>Then decide together whether discovery makes sense. No project commitment required.</p><a class="text-link" href="pricing.html">Review the offer first ↗</a></aside><div><form class="intake-form" id="preview-form"><label for="problem">What needs a clearer next step?</label><select id="problem" name="problem"><option value="Missed calls and enquiries">Missed calls and enquiries</option><option value="Quote follow-up">Quote follow-up</option><option value="Customer or owner updates">Customer or owner updates</option><option value="Something else">Something else</option></select><label for="example">What happened last time? <span class="tiny">(optional)</span></label><textarea id="example" name="example" maxlength="1200" placeholder="Use a fictional example here. No personal or customer details."></textarea><button class="pill" type="submit">Preview the next step <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><p class="tiny">Nothing is sent or saved. No calendar, CRM or backend is connected.</p></form><section class="preview-result" id="preview-result" hidden tabindex="-1" aria-live="polite"><h2>A clearer place to start.</h2><p data-result-summary></p><p>This is where a live site would offer a fit call. This concept hasn’t sent a request or booked anything.</p><a class="text-link" href="how-it-works.html">See what happens after a fit call ↗</a></section></div></div></div>''')

